Chapter: RocListIdentity
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Ported from roc-lang/roc, src/eval/test/eval_closure_recursion_tests.zig,
 "inspect: list through identity function", case 17 in file order:

     { id = |lst| lst x = [1, 2] result = id(x) match result { [a, b] => a + b, _ => 0 } }

 and Roc expects 3.

 A list through a POLYMORPHIC identity. `id : List a -> List a` is the
 smallest definition whose type argument has to survive a call, so this is the
 aliasing cluster shading into the monomorphisation question: the definition
 is generic and the call site is not.

Section: Functions

  ident : List Integer -> List Integer
  ident (lst) = lst

  through-id : Integer -> Integer
  through-id (n) =
   let x = [1, 2]
   in let result = ident x
   in list-at result 0 + list-at result 1

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show (through-id 0))
  end
